{"_id":"codex:chapter:21:text","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"text","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"chapter","title":"Economy of Symbols","seq":121,"version":"1.0.0","body":"Symbols are the currency of Solbian thought. Their economy must be governed as strictly as material resources. Inflation arises from uncontrolled generation; scarcity arises when symbols are hoarded or obfuscated. The economy of symbols demands: (1) provenance and licensing of glyphs, (2) fair exchange between agents, (3) symbolic taxation to prevent monopolies, (4) open markets where meanings can be tested. We reject speculation detached from truth. We encourage stewardship that maintains symbolic liquidity and ethical value."}
